.SH GPU MANAGEMENT
Manage GPU resources.

.TP
.B nunet gpu list
List all available GPUs with detailed information including model, VRAM, vendor, PCI address, UUID, and index.

.TP
.B nunet gpu test
Test GPU by running a Docker container with GPU resources. Automatically selects the GPU with maximum free VRAM.

.SH NETWORK UTILITY
Network utility tool for managing deployment networks.

.TP
.B nunet network ls [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
List all deployment networks the DMS is part of.
.RS
.TP
\fB-c, --context\fR \fISTRING\fR
Specify a capability context (required).
.TP
\fB-v, --verbose\fR
Enable verbose output showing allocation and network details.
.RE

.TP
.B nunet network show [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Show details of a specific network.
.RS
.TP
\fB-c, --context\fR \fISTRING\fR
Capability context (required).
.TP
\fB-i, --id\fR \fISTRING\fR
Deployment/Ensemble ID (required).
.RE

.TP
.B nunet network attach [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Attach to a deployment network. Currently only ssh supported.
.RS
.TP
\fB-c, --context\fR \fISTRING\fR
Capability context (required).
.TP
\fB-i, --id\fR \fISTRING\fR
Deployment ID (required).
.TP
\fB-a, --alloc\fR \fISTRING\fR
Allocation ID (required).
.TP
\fB--shell\fR
Open an SSH shell to the allocation.
.TP
\fB--forward\fR
Set up port forwarding. (Not Implemented)
.TP
\fB--username\fR \fISTRING\fR
SSH username.
.TP
\fB--identity\fR \fISTRING\fR
SSH private key file path.
.TP
\fB--port\fR \fISTRING\fR
Port to attach to. SSH listening port in case of --shell
.TP
\fB--port-map\fR \fISTRING\fR
Port mapping configuration. (Not Implemented)
.RE

.SH RUN THE DEVICE MANAGEMENT SERVICE

.TP
.B nunet run [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Start the Device Management Service (DMS). The DMS is a system application for running a node in the NuNet decentralized network of compute providers. By default, DMS listens on port 9999.
.RS
.TP
\fB-c, --context\fR \fISTRING\fR
Capability context name (default: "dms").
.RE

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Generate a new keypair:
.B nunet key new mykey
.TP
Retrieve the DID associated with a key:
.B nunet key did mykey
.TP
Create a Ledger alias:
.B nunet key ledger-alias set business 3
.TP
Start the DMS:
.B nunet run
.TP
List available GPUs:
.B nunet gpu list
.TP
Test GPU deployment:
.B nunet gpu test
.TP
Create a new capability context:
.B nunet cap new mycapability
.TP
Add a "provide" anchor to a capability context:
.B nunet cap anchor --context mycapability --provide '{"action": "read"}'
.TP
Delegate a capability to another DID:
.B nunet cap delegate did:example:123 --cap /public --topic /nunet/public
.TP
Revoke a capability token:
.B nunet cap revoke --context user '{"some": "json", "token": "here"}'
.TP
Remove a capability anchor:
.B nunet cap remove --context user --root did:key:abcd1234
.TP
List networks:
.B nunet network ls --context dms
.TP
Show network details:
.B nunet network show --context dms --id deployment123
.TP
Attach to network allocation:
.B nunet network attach --shell --context dms --id deployment123 --alloc alloc1
.TP
Construct and send a message to an actor:
.B nunet actor msg /public/hello 'Hello, World!' --dest did:example:456 | nunet actor send
.TP
Invoke a predefined command on an actor:
.B nunet actor cmd --context dms /dms/node/peers/list

.SH NOTES
.IP \[bu] 2
Some commands may require root privileges.
.IP \[bu]
Be cautious when configuring network settings to avoid disrupting network connectivity.
.IP \[bu]
Keep private keys secure, as they provide access to your identity and associated capabilities within the NuNet DMS.

.SH SEE ALSO
For more detailed information on specific commands, use the \fB--help\fR option with any command.

.SH AUTHOR
Written and maintained by Gustavo Silva <gustavo.silva@nunet.io>.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DMS_PASSPHRASE
If set, this environment variable shares the passphrase across all cryptographic keys stored, avoiding interactive prompts. Use with caution to prevent exposing the passphrase.

.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report bugs to the NuNet issue tracker at <https://gitlab.com/nunet/device-management-service/-/issues>
